ent  things I had a ton of energy I remember  I would make up dances with my friends  and like choreograph stuff in the living  room and then I would go and I remember  actually having Encyclopedia Brittanica  and like copying it down and like  rewriting the content making new  pictures and creating things so as a  little girl I was always wanting to  learn new things do new things and  create stuff you know I was cheerleader  so I was and by the way I wasn't a  cheerleader for a while I got rejected  so many times I tried out I can't even  tell you I would practice in my living  room I'd put the video camera up to try  and like figure out why my arm wasn't  straight enough  but I always just wanted to express  myself in all these different ways and  when you know my parents kept these  great books of when I was little where  you kind of record what your kids want  and what they're into and all those  things and I remember in the section  where it says well what do you want to  be when you grow up  it was always five to seven things it  was never just one thing and they were  all completely different it was like  from dancer to teacher to model to  actress to writer like all these  different kind of professions that  sounded fascinating to me so that was me  when I was little I was all over the  place  now I have a special bonus clip from  Murray on how to take risks that I think  you're gonna enjoy but before that is  time for the three-point landing  questions let's go from just watching  the video to taking an action here we go  question number one what is your go-to  mantra number two where do you need to  be more consistent and number three  what's the standard that you need to  raise in your business or your life and  if you like this video and will take  action after watching it give me a hash  tag believe down the comments as well  after I look left Wall Street I went on  a bit of an odyssey to figure out what I  was supposed to do and I just went back  to m